{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/check-loa.sh","line":75,"code_snippet":"elif [[ \"$submodule_mount\" == \"true\" && -f \".loa/${file}\" ]]; then\n  not_mounted=$((not_mounted + 1))","reasoning_trace":"submodule_mount is the heuristic [[ -d .loa/.claude ]] (:64). Upstream holds every manifest path, so in a submodule mount an absent path is always informational not-mounted and Missing can never fire; a removed link to a hook or gate script is indistinguishable from a by-design unlinked path. The heuristic is also satisfiable in a non-submodule mount by creating .loa/.claude/ plus a shadow copy. DISS-C-002 part 2 (`return 0` hides drift) is not a defect: fail() increments FAILURES (:36) and main exits 1 when FAILURES > 0 (:603-605); the base's trailing `[[ ]] && log` returned 1 and aborted the script under set -e.","finding":"In submodule mode the integrity check degrades to a Tampered-only check; deletion of a linked System Zone file is never reported as Missing.","critique":"The outcome is the #1267 design decision, but it should be compared against the mount's own link list rather than against existence upstream.","remediation":"Record the set of linked paths at mount time (mount-submodule.sh) and treat an absent path that is in that set as Missing; keep not-mounted for paths outside it.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/354.html"]}
