{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/fingerprint.sh","line":54,"code_snippet":"else BATS_BIN=\"$HOME/.local/dotfiles/tools/diff-so-fancy/test/bats/bin/bats\"; fi","reasoning_trace":"Operator-specific fallback path under $HOME in shared code; $HOME under set -u; tool_version executes it when present (:60-62). pipeline-run.sh:428 swallows a failure (|| echo \"\") and records fingerprint null. Confirmed by cross-model review DISS-C-005.","finding":"The fingerprint executes a binary from a user-writable, operator-specific path and silently records null when the script fails.","critique":"A missing bats should read bats=absent, as the header promises for other tools.","remediation":"Drop the dotfiles fallback (bats=absent when not on PATH) and make pipeline-run.sh fail or warn when fingerprint.sh exits non-zero.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/426.html"]}
