{"id":"ARCH-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"standards_compliance","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/defaults/model-config.yaml","line":144,"code_snippet":"# PLACEHOLDER: gpt-5.5 list prices copied 2026-10-15 until the gpt-6.1 rate card is confirmed","reasoning_trace":"gpt-6.1-sol pricing (:144-149) is an acknowledged placeholder; codex-headless cli_model now points at it (:240) so every codex estimate and MODELINV row prices through it with no provisional marker on the rows. The entry's fallback_chain is openai:codex-headless (:135), whose cli_model is gpt-6.1-sol, so an API-key failure silently re-runs the request through the operator's ChatGPT subscription (cross-model DISS-C-006; review DISS-C-003).","finding":"Placeholder pricing flows into cost rows unmarked, and the HTTP entry's fallback crosses into the subscription credential path on API errors.","critique":"The within-company chain is the repository convention, but the placeholder should be visible where it is consumed.","remediation":"Add a pricing_note/provisional flag that pricing.py surfaces on rows, or price the hop as unknown until the rate card lands; track the bead named in the comment.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
