{"id":"CQ-005","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":857,"code_snippet":"if [[ \"$timed_out\" == false ]] && { [[ $rc -eq 143 ]] || [[ $rc -eq 137 ]] || ... }; then finish interrupted 4","reasoning_trace":"docker run --memory 4g (:688) OOM-kills the CLI with exit 137 before the timeout; the driver classes it interrupted (exit 4) rather than agent_error.","finding":"A model that blows the memory cap reads as an operator interrupt and is excluded from the analysis as interrupted.","critique":"Distinguish the container's OOMKilled flag from a signal.","remediation":"Inspect `docker inspect --format '{{.State.OOMKilled}}'` before --rm removes the container (drop --rm and remove manually), or treat 137 without a driver signal as agent_error.","confidence":"medium","references":[]}
