{"id":"SEC-010","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":770,"code_snippet":"ledger_micro=\"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$ledger_rows\" | jq -R -n '[inputs | fromjson? | select(type == \"object\") | (.cost_micro_usd // ((.cost_usd // 0) * 1000000))] | add // 0 | round' ...","reasoning_trace":"sandbox/.eval/cost-ledger.jsonl is writable by the agent under test; rows are summed into SPENT_MICRO (:854) with no non-negative or numeric clamp. A negative or non-numeric cost_micro_usd row lowers the recorded spend and defers cap_failure (:864); a huge one triggers it.","finding":"The per-run spend cap trusts ledger rows the sandbox agent can write.","critique":"The CLI's result.total_cost_usd is authoritative; the ledger should only add.","remediation":"Clamp each row to a non-negative number (`select(type == \"number\" and . >= 0)`) and count rows by cheval's primitive_id shape only.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html"]}
